# Singly Linked List — Insertion

Insertion means **adding a new node** to a singly linked list.

There are **3 types of insertion**:

```text
Insertion
   │
   ├── 1. At First
   ├── 2. At Last
   └── 3. In Between
1. Insertion at First

A new node is inserted before the current head.

Cases
Case 1: head == NULL
head → NULL

Insert 10

head → [10 | NULL]
Case 2: Nodes already exist
Before:

head → 10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Insert 5:

After:

head → 5 → 10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
Main Logic
temp->next = head;
head = temp;
2. Insertion at Last

A new node is inserted at the end of the linked list.

Cases
Case 1: head == NULL
head → NULL

Insert 10

head → 10 → NULL
head = temp;
Case 2: n > 0 Nodes
Before:

head → 10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Insert 40:

After:

head → 10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL
Find the Last Node
while (temp->next != NULL)
{
    temp = temp->next;
}

temp->next = newNode;
3. Insertion in Between

Insert a new node after a targeted value.

Cases
Case 1: List is Empty
head → NULL

"No nodes are there"
Case 2: Target Not Found
10 → 20 → 30 → NULL

Target = 50

"Targeted node doesn't exist"
Case 3: Target Found
Before:

10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
      ↑
    target

Insert 25

After:

10 → 20 → 25 → 30 → NULL
Main Logic
newNode->next = temp->next;
temp->next = newNode;
Full Code — Insertion
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Node
{
public:
    int value;
    Node *next;

    Node(int value)
    {
        this->value = value;
        this->next = NULL;
    }
};

class SinglyLinkedList
{
private:
    Node *head;

public:

    SinglyLinkedList()
    {
        this->head = NULL;
    }

    // 1. INSERTION AT FIRST
    void insertAtFirst(int data)
    {
        Node *temp = new Node(data);

        // Case 1 and Case 2
        temp->next = head;
        head = temp;
    }


    // 2. INSERTION AT LAST
    void insertAtLast(int data)
    {
        Node *newNode = new Node(data);

        // Case 1: No node
        if (head == NULL)
        {
            head = newNode;
            return;
        }

        // Case 2: n nodes
        Node *temp = head;

        while (temp->next != NULL)
        {
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        temp->next = newNode;
    }


    // 3. INSERTION IN BETWEEN
    void insertInBetween(int data, int targetedValue)
    {
        // Case 1: No node
        if (head == NULL)
        {
            cout << "Nodes are not there" << endl;
            return;
        }

        Node *temp = head;

        // Find target
        while (temp != NULL &&
               temp->value != targetedValue)
        {
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // Case 2: Target not found
        if (temp == NULL)
        {
            cout << "Targeted node doesn't exist" << endl;
            return;
        }

        // Case 3: Target found
        Node *newNode = new Node(data);

        newNode->next = temp->next;
        temp->next = newNode;
    }


    // DISPLAY
    void display()
    {
        if (head == NULL)
        {
            cout << "No nodes exist" << endl;
            return;
        }

        Node *temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL)
        {
            cout << temp->value << " ";
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        cout << endl;
    }
};


int main()
{
    SinglyLinkedList obj;

    obj.insertAtFirst(10);
    obj.insertAtFirst(20);

    obj.insertAtLast(30);

    obj.insertInBetween(25, 20);

    obj.display();

    return 0;
}
